      "math_academy_id": "e-1102",
      "problem": "What is the domain of the function $f(x)$ defined by the following table? \n\n| $x$ | $\\,-2\\,$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,4\\,$ | $\\,6\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $-2$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $2$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The domain is the set of all input values for which the function is defined. In the table, this corresponds to the set of $x$-values in the first row:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\{ -2,-1,0,2,4,6\\}\n$$",
